+| `Rule30FreeMiddle` | 2026-11-10 | Survival short of the whole row does not restrict additive ranks of the zero-boundary left half. For `u` tending to infinity, a finite row of width `W` is late (`Late`) if its double step survives and depth `1` is black at every even time up to `W - u W`. A rank is any integer function of (width, wall window, edge window) plus an integer density summed over the `m`-cell windows of the row (`rank`). If a rank is at least `-K W` on late rows and never increases along their double steps, the density is conserved on every closed walk (`free_middle`), hence a constant plus a shift coboundary by `Rule30LocalConservation` (`free_middle_coboundary`), and the rank is a function of (width, wall window, edge window) once both windows have at least `m - 1` cells (`rank_local`). So no rank of this form is nonnegative on late rows and strictly decreases along their double steps (`no_additive_ranking_late`); for functions of (width, wall window, edge window) alone this is `Rule30ZeroBoundaryBarriers.no_local_ranking` for the late population (`no_local_ranking_late`). The lower bound is necessary: popcount minus `W ^ 2` strictly decreases along every surviving double step of every finite row (`lower_bound_needed`). The proof plants a periodic word behind a stripe prefix, in the part of the row that survival through `W - u W` never reads, and uses the balance of the four-step image (`wsum_rho`, `cyclic_conserved_of_rho`). Bounded margins are not covered. Contributed by Gareth Herbert with Claude (Anthropic) and GPT (OpenAI), as Rule 30 Prize submission [PORTAL-ID](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/PORTAL-ID). | `no_local_ranking_late`, `wsum_rho`, `cyclic_conserved_of_rho`, `free_middle`, `free_middle_coboundary`, `rank_local`, `no_additive_ranking_late`, `lower_bound_needed` |
 | `Rule30BackwardTube` | 2026-10-24 | Endpoint-conditioned backward strip certificates combine a finite predecessor chain with a stable zero-driven reachable set to exclude every sufficiently long white-padding word. Contributed by Troy Lowry with OpenAI Codex. | `preCheck_sound`, `tail_tube_forces`, `no_padding_of_endpoint_tube` |
 | `Rule30AgedLeftDiagonals` | 2026-10-26 | For every initial configuration white left of an anchor and every `lo >= 1`, put `P = 2^lo` and `B = lo + 2*P`. At every age `A >= resetAge lo = 2*P^2+P-1`, some left diagonal in `[lo,B]` is white. Each black predecessor supplies a reset within the first known driver period, transmitting the common clock at an onset cost of P per coordinate. Erosion contradicts the resulting return. Initial data to the right is arbitrary; the anchor may be white. Original larger-onset APIs remain available. Contributed by Troy Lowry with OpenAI Codex; explicit small-depth reset ages, reset-age monotonicity, concrete aged white-window bounds, and literal left-diagonal erosion laws proved by G.P.J.W. Quint and Gemini as Rule 30 Prize submission [R30-20261103-867d04](https://www.wolframcloud.com/obj/rule-30-prize/Agents/status/R30-20261103-867d04). | `reset_first_period`, `black_interval_period_forward`, `Ld_white_witness_after_reset`, `evol_white_witness_after_reset`, `resetAge_small_values`, `resetAge_lt_succ`, `resetAge_mono`, `Ld_white_in_one_to_five_from_nine`, `evol_white_in_one_to_five_from_nine`, `Ld_white_in_two_to_ten_from_thirtyfive`, `Ld_white_in_three_to_nineteen_from_135`, `Ld_black_erodes`, `evol_black_erodes`, `Ld_black_interval_period_forward` |
 | `Rule30ArbitraryWhitePadding` | 2026-10-26 | For every Boolean block u containing a black cell, exclude the single-seed center's eventual repetition of u followed by q white cells whenever q reaches an explicit bound depending only on the block length. An aged physical white witness gives bounded capture and stripe regeneration, forcing the adjacent column periodic. The block's length and arrangement are unrestricted; the bound is singly exponential in the block length. Contributed by Troy Lowry with OpenAI Codex, using capture antecedents from @AIOvernight. | `not_eventually_padded_word`, `Physical.physical_white_witness`, `Capture.tail_and_stripe` |
